{"ts": "2026-10-17T15:28:05.956579Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T1514Z-dc70", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-heavy-path-spans", "seq": 37, "type": "task.done", "task": "4.1", "base": "7e32290828392d032b6c195e16d56044f3e98f52", "parents": [], "notes": "Q-001: applied the answer's edit to the unfrozen packages/cli/tests/test_telemetry_cli_heavy_paths.py (order the two index-tree spans by start_time, keep all assertions). F-8f538f: telemetry.span's kind is typed str (unknown values map to INTERNAL), so the 'bogus' kind test type-checks under mypy strict with no cast/ignore. F-b98cfc: the failure scenarios are now decidable and implemented/tested - ConversionError gives convert outcome=failed + ERROR error.type=ConversionError (test_conversion_failure_span_is_failed), VisionError gives caption outcome=failed + ERROR error.type=VisionError (test_caption_failure_span_is_failed), caught CoChangeUnavailable gives cochange outcome=unavailable with no ERROR (test_cochange_unavailable_is_an_outcome_not_an_error), and index-tree asserts files.scanned/added/updated/unchanged/failed (test_index_tree_counter_attributes_track_updated_and_unchanged). Implementation: command_span lives in telemetry.py and marshals SystemExit/typer.Exit exit codes (non-zero, string or None -> ERROR; code 0 stays UNSET). index_tree wraps the whole walk in mintmory.index_tree.scan (per-file co-change embeddings stay inside it), the --prune pass in .prune, and the post-walk block in .cochange (outcome=ok + changesets, or unavailable on CoChangeUnavailable). mintmory.convert wraps extract_markdown only when want_binary; mintmory.vision.caption wraps captioner.describe. ingest wraps every extract_markdown. The file_span helper sets suffix/size_bytes up front and outcome on exit, marking failures with mark_error and re-raising so the existing ConversionError/VisionError handlers still count them. Only main.py, telemetry.py and the human-unfrozen test file changed.", "suppressions": [{"file": "packages/core/src/mintmory/core/telemetry.py", "line": 1017, "rule": "BLE001", "reason": "Setting an attribute in the new file_span helper must never raise into the wrapped converter/captioner."}, {"file": "packages/core/src/mintmory/core/telemetry.py", "line": 1072, "rule": "type: ignore[return-value]", "reason": "wraps-based wrapper returned as _F in the new command_span, matching the other decorators in this module."}, {"file": "packages/cli/src/mintmory/cli/main.py", "line": 796, "rule": "S101", "reason": "Pre-existing suppression, relocated only by reindenting the index-tree walk under mintmory.index_tree.scan; not newly added."}, {"file": "packages/cli/src/mintmory/cli/main.py", "line": 848, "rule": "S101", "reason": "Pre-existing suppression, relocated only by reindenting the index-tree walk under mintmory.index_tree.scan; not newly added."}]}
